        {
          "id": 825991118,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "[inputMask : QString](https://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qlineedit.html#inputMask-prop) - `<string>900000000</string>` is a character mask, not a numeric value.  \n```\n| Mask Character | Meaning                                                                     |\n|----------------|-----------------------------------------------------------------------------|\n| 9              | character of the Number category required, e.g 0-9.                         |\n| 0              | character of the Number category permitted but not required.                |\n```\n`QIntValidator(0,999999999,this)` should cover the same range of values.  \n  \nIdeally, instead of allowing the user to enter a very large number, we would pop up a message with a link to `editcap` and remind them that life would be better with more, smaller files. :-)  \n  \n[Display Filter Reference: Frame](https://www.wireshark.org/docs/dfref/f/frame.html)  \n`frame.number\tFrame Number\tUnsigned integer, 4 bytes\t1.0.0 to 3.6.1`  \n  \nIs this syntax ok: ([syntax_line_edit.cpp#L46](https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/blob/master/ui/qt/widgets/syntax_line_edit.cpp#L46))  \n`std::numeric_limits<quint32>::max()`",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
