        {
          "id": 826003585,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "The other gotcha is this concept of \"Intermediate\" values that the validator allows to pass through - ugh!  \nhttps://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qvalidator.html  \n  \nI agree that hard coding the value to \"999999999\" is not pretty but to properly implement it using `max()` will require reworking the code to only accept the keypress for \"Acceptable\" values.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0809ffc6d9d98013a1895132bc055c622830b8a20bfa49328f53d5eb4a1206cb?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/chuckcraft"
