        {
          "id": 826332513,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Integer values are derived from base-system values. Thats why you should avoid data types like \"unsigned int\" in general if doing cross-plattform development and keep to values like \"quint32\". This ensures, that it is always the same size (32 bit in this case, and set by the plattform toolkit (qt here). Other possible values would be defined in stdint.h, where you could use uint32_t for example as a 4-byte unsigned integer, which will be set to \"unsigned int\" on a windows plattform.\n\nOne famous example why you should got with well-defined data types (and int is by NO MEANS well-defined in cross-plattform development), are the pointer sizes on 32-bit and 64-bit windows. On *nix for example, they are allways 8-byte long when you are operating on a 64-bit plattform. 4-byte on a 32-bit plattform. On Windows it strongly depends on the context of your application execution, so for instance in the beginning of moving to 64-bit, all console applications where using 4-byte pointers even if executed on 64-bit. That makes pointer arithmetic a nice little adventure.\n\nSome embedded examples see even the datatype char being 2-byte and so on.\n\nSo, to abbreviate, if the upper limit is not really an issue, just limiting to 4-byte, I would go with ->setRange and set it to 0 and quint32 max respectivly. Why quint32? Because it leaves Qt the headache of figuring out the correct datatype underneath and avoids you picking a type which might result in an issue on a different plattform.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/9e1d973c5007651b2ca47071f80324c2de5349d873e365cf0761df5542dfe382?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/rknall"
          },
          "created_at": "2022-01-31T09:13:25.978Z",
          "updated_at": "2022-01-31T09:13:25.978Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 137717612,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
