        {
          "id": 826335554,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "> \"typically\" doesn't inspire a lot of confidence in what may happen in the future.\n\nI understand. But in this case, I would just stick with it. Either set the upper value explicitly or just set the bottom value to 0. Both are fine. As written above in longer form - figuring out the correct size of an int on all plattforms supported can be tricky business, which is why it is written as \"typically\". It just means, if int is indead just 4-bytes long, that that value is correct for a 4-byte signed integer.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2498449,
            "username": "rknall",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Roland Knall",
            "state": "active",
